  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_Final_Review_Q03
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: In the Security log, why filter for Audit Failure rather than reading
    everything?
  choices:
  - Audit Success entries are not recorded by default
  - Failures are the short list worth reading; successes are thousands of normal
    events
  - Audit Failure entries are deleted after 24 hours
  - Only failures contain the user name
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: Every normal sign-in and every permitted file open is an Audit Success.
    The refusals are the ones that say something.
